From a88141ba0853fb22d94e21ce257b75391a051112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meshoklv <119141917+meshoklv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:59:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: hot SMC write windows (exp/hot-smc-v2,
 FEX_HOT_SMC_PAGES=2, default off)

v1 checked every instruction on a hot page and stopped re-arming its trap.
Its DS3 run had 0 check failures on 11,069 checked instructions, so v2
checks only instructions overlapping the 16-byte blocks the protector was
seen writing, keeps the stock write trap, and turns a trap at a known
window into a fast trap (un-protect without invalidation). Unknown
addresses on a hot page are learned and invalidate the page as before; a
periodic audit re-arms all hot pages. Burst (decrypt) and wide writers are
not marked.

